    },
    {
      "id": "d0ab767b735e9181440f93e67d79d55ec66a87fd",
      "tag": "autogenerated:ai-review",
      "author": {
        "_account_id": 1345,
        "name": "Gerrit AI review for Lustre",
        "display_name": "AI review",
        "email": "gaireview@linuxhacker.ru",
        "username": "aireview",
        "status": "Contact Oleg Drokin (green@whamcloud.com) with any questions on this account"
      },
      "date": "2026-11-24 09:32:57.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 2:\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nLooks good; the new gate matches the commit that added the MDT-side lustre.pin mapping, and no re-spin is needed.\n\n(suggestion) The test skip is correct, but it also hides a real interop gap. llapi_pcc_pin_file() and llapi_pcc_unpin_file() now always use XATTR_LUSTRE_PIN, with no fallback. As a result, `lfs pcc pin` and `lfs pcc unpin` from a master client always fail with EOPNOTSUPP against a 2.16 MDT, even for root. Before 84100d7f7d this worked through trusted.pin. Should liblustreapi retry with XATTR_NAME_PIN on -EOPNOTSUPP, which keeps the old root-only behaviour on older MDTs? That could go in a separate patch under this ticket.",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 2
    },
